rt of conundrum  he told you he was a swiss banker he'd  got various different business interests  he was also  an mi6 spy at what stage  did things begin to unravel for you and  you start to uncover  who he really was  well it wasn't really until uh well into  i've been in the relationship for about  a year very miserable for most of it i  mean it was  very very exciting for the first two or  three months  and then became he started to isolate me  and i  became more and more depressed and  introverted um  and it probably wasn't until another  year when  actually i hadn't seen him for a while  he by that stage had claimed to  have a brain tumor and have had an  operation on that  um staging a very convincing  little charade to make me believe that  that had happened and that was a one of  a number of charades that he he did  stage to back up his claims  um but i think it wasn't until then and  eventually when he failed to show up  when we hadn't seen each other  for about six months and had arranged to  meet in nice  and he didn't show and i just thought  you know  nobody could do this no one claiming to  love someone could just leave them and i  was in a terrible state myself by that  stage  and i just thought no this this is this  is all wrong  because not only had you lost all of  your  life savings you'd also lost a lot of  yourself this took a huge mental toll on  you  did um i think the the isolation  uh was was really terrible and i mean i  was having panic attacks and nightmares  i felt complicit in my own downfall  in retrospect once i found out who he  was because right at the beginning of  the relationship he had  sort of sworn me to secrecy and said  that it would take him 18 months to  extricate himself from his contract with  um  mi6 and he asked me to give  give him my word that i would that i  could be strong and stand by him and i  did that  um and sadly so the sort of character  traits that i  thought of as my strengths of loyalty  and discretion  